nai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":6,"section_title":"Exponential smoothing for every partial deck","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:63e648a75527320e339eea45cf86e72c780522886e8ff81552a2fa24a33fa371","file":"preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/05-strong-providers.tex","line":35,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"c3de3e10413ce34e6579b07d4adf96b0884c18d97844a7d5d73ee5dbab5da622","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/05-strong-providers.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:63e648a75527320e339eea45cf86e72c780522886e8ff81552a2fa24a33fa371","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/05-strong-providers.tex#L35"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{n:strong-density}\nThere are absolute constants $p\\in(1,2]$ and $C<\\infty$ such that,\nfor every $N=2^d$, every coordinate order, every $0\\le l\\le N$,\neither choice of $H_N$, and every $x\\in\\mathcal X_{N,l}$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{n:strong-injection-density}\n \\frac1{(N)_l}\\sum_{y\\in\\mathcal X_{N,l}}\n       \\big((N)_lH_N(x,y)\\big)^p\\le e^{Cl}.\n\\end{equation}\nAfter increasing $C$, the same constants give\n\\begin{equation}\\label{n:strong-density-power-normalization}\n N^{-l}\\sum_{y\\in\\{0,1\\}^{dl}}\n       \\big(N^lH_N(x,y)\\big)^p\\le e^{Cl},\n\\end{equation}\nwhere the kernel is extended by zero on tuples with repeated positions.\nBoth conclusions hold with rows replaced by columns."}
